jdns
------------------------------------------
JDNS is a simple DNS implementation that can perform normal DNS queries of any
record type (notably SRV), as well as Multicast DNS queries and advertising.
Multicast support is based on Jeremie Miller's 'mdnsd' implementation.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libQt5Core-devel-5.9.4-2
  libQt5Core5-5.9.4-2
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libjdns-devel-3.1.3-1bl1
  libjdns3-3.1.3-1bl1
  libqjdns-devel-3.1.3-1bl1
  libqjdns3-3.1.3-1bl1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libQt5Core-devel-5.9.4-2
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/psi-im/jdns

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/psi-im/jdns/archive/refs/tags/v3.1.3.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack jdns-3.1.3-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./jdns-3.1.3-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/jdns-3.1.3-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/jdns-3.1.3-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libjdns3-3.1.3-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libjdns-devel-3.1.3-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libqjdns3-3.1.3-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libqjdns-devel-3.1.3-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

